			<div class="content" id="post-content-3914817">
									

<p>I really, really enjoyed this. The weird details like the anomaly not affecting people with severed digits was a good start, I honestly enjoyed the description alone enough to upvote this. While I liked the first interview, I was afraid there was going to become a case of too much extra content bringing down the concise and solid main description, but then the escalation of the effect and the story that was told sucked me in.</p>
<p>I love that it gives enough description of the cult to keep us interested without giving everything away. My only quibble is that I feel the Foundation using D-Class from the area where SCP-3873 came from seems like a serious oversight, but you could fix that by making it so the D-Class was recruited from somewhere else in the USA, maybe with a name change, and it wasn't initially apparent he came from Florida. Also, there's a broken collapsible in the addendum area.</p>
<p>Easy upvote and I really hope this gets the attention it deserves because it is a masterwork of an SCP.</p>

