					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nightmarechameleon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2912806); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2912806&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606142506" alt="Nightmarechameleon" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2912806)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nightmarechameleon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2912806); return false;" >Nightmarechameleon</a></span> <span class="odate time_1571312488 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">17 Oct 2019 11:41</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4400583">
									

<p>This article is well written, but still has some issues. Here are some fixes.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Issue: There's no way in hell the foundation is going to leave a D-class alone with a largely defenseless anomaly.</p>
<p>Solution: Add cameras to the cell, have security notice and barge in. Don't even have to change all that much.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Issue: D-class being a cult member is a very large plot hole, for a few reasons. First off, according to cult, falling in love is taboo. Having him be loyal enough to try and kill her, but unloyal enough to fall in love himself is bad writing. Unless he's a later cult member, she'd probably spot him from meetings.</p>
<p>Solution: have the D-class be fully unrelated to her. Perhaps have them get into an argument, or just have him attack her because he's a violent criminal.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Issue: Agent whatshisname receiving the curse.</p>
<p>Solution: Have it jump to the surgeon who removed her arms. Simple, obvious, brutal.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>There's some other issues, such as &quot;Anomaly chick falling in love with everyone she meets&quot; and the direct jump to the note from DR. French (add an introduction maybe).</p>
<p>+1 to save this joint from deletion. It's got hella potential, you just need to act</p>

							</div>

